-- Q23 [Gas Exchange & Pulmonary Circulation] easy skill1 ans=C
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Respiratory System', 'Gas Exchange & Pulmonary Circulation', 'As venous blood passes through a systemic capillary bed, carbon dioxide produced by the tissues enters the red blood cells and plasma and is transported to the lungs in several chemical forms. In a healthy person at rest, which form accounts for the largest fraction of the total CO2 carried in the blood?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "CO2 physically dissolved in the plasma"}, {"label": "B", "text": "Carbaminohemoglobin formed by CO2 bound to the globin chains of hemoglobin"}, {"label": "C", "text": "Bicarbonate ions dissolved in the plasma and red blood cells"}, {"label": "D", "text": "Carbonic acid circulating intact in the plasma"}]'::jsonb, 'C', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Organ Systems.'' The answer is C because roughly 70% of the CO2 transported in the blood travels as bicarbonate ion: CO2 diffuses into red blood cells, where carbonic anhydrase converts it to carbonic acid, which dissociates into H+ and HCO3-, and the bicarbonate then moves out into the plasma (with the chloride shift maintaining electrical balance). (Choice C) is correct: bicarbonate is the dominant transport form, carrying about 70% of total CO2. (Choice A) is incorrect: only a small fraction, roughly 7-10%, of CO2 is carried physically dissolved in the plasma, so this is a minority form, not the majority. (Choice B) is incorrect: carbaminohemoglobin, CO2 bound to amino groups of the globin portion of hemoglobin, accounts for only about 20-23% of CO2 transport, more than the dissolved fraction but well short of bicarbonate. (Choice D) is incorrect: carbonic acid is only a transient intermediate that rapidly dissociates into H+ and bicarbonate; it does not accumulate or circulate intact as a major carrier. This question requires the skill of recalling the relative proportions of the three forms of CO2 transport and identifying bicarbonate as the predominant form.', 'easy', '3B', 'Organ Systems', 'biology', 1, 60)
  RETURNING id
)
