-- Q36 [Exhalation & Elastic Recoil] medium skill4 ans=D
WITH q AS (
  INSERT INTO questions (section, topic, subtopic, question_text, options, correct_answer, explanation, difficulty, foundation, content_category, discipline, cognitive_skill, estimated_time_seconds)
  VALUES ('bio_biochem', 'The Respiratory System', 'Exhalation & Elastic Recoil', 'Two excised lungs are inflated stepwise, and for each the transpulmonary pressure needed to add a fixed 0.5 L of volume is recorded. A healthy lung requires a 2 cm H2O rise in transpulmonary pressure to add that 0.5 L, whereas a fibrotic lung requires a 5 cm H2O rise to add the same 0.5 L. Which statement correctly characterizes the fibrotic lung relative to the healthy lung?', '[{"label": "A", "text": "The fibrotic lung has higher compliance, because a larger transpulmonary pressure change is needed to produce the same volume change."}, {"label": "B", "text": "The fibrotic lung has lower compliance, because the same transpulmonary pressure change produces a larger volume change."}, {"label": "C", "text": "The fibrotic lung has higher compliance, because the same transpulmonary pressure change produces a larger volume change."}, {"label": "D", "text": "The fibrotic lung has lower compliance, because a larger transpulmonary pressure change is needed to produce the same volume change."}]'::jsonb, 'D', 'This is a Biology question that falls under the content category ''Organ Systems.'' The answer is D because compliance is defined as the change in volume divided by the change in transpulmonary pressure (C = ΔV/ΔP); a stiff, fibrotic lung that demands a larger pressure change (5 cm H2O) to achieve the identical 0.5 L volume change has a smaller ΔV/ΔP ratio and therefore lower compliance than the healthy lung, which needs only 2 cm H2O for the same volume. (Choice D) is correct: it pairs the correct direction (lower compliance) with the correct reasoning—more pressure is required per unit of volume added, which is exactly a reduced ΔV/ΔP. (Choice A) is incorrect: although its reasoning (larger pressure change needed for the same volume) is true, it draws the wrong conclusion; requiring more pressure per unit volume is the hallmark of LOW compliance (high elastance), not high compliance. (Choice B) is incorrect: it reaches the correct conclusion (lower compliance) but with a false premise—the fibrotic lung does not produce a larger volume change for the same pressure; it produces a smaller volume change per unit pressure. (Choice C) is incorrect: both parts are wrong—the fibrotic lung is less compliant, not more, and it yields a smaller (not larger) volume change for a given pressure change. This question tests the skill of applying the quantitative definition of compliance (ΔV/ΔP) to distinguish a stiff, low-compliance lung from a normal one.', 'medium', '3B', 'Organ Systems', 'biology', 4, 90)
  RETURNING id
)
